
This is a personal quant repo. The goal is to drive quantitative trading with periodic GitHub Actions runs. But the exchange's software depends on Windows,
and I do not know whether a GitHub Windows container + my quant account credentials can run it.
The architecture can be validated on my local machine first, and then I can try driving it with GitHub Actions.


Please re-learn the current architecture, and also consider the following questions:
1 Confirm whether brokers (e.g. Guojin Securities) still offer miniQMT. If they do, we can run with WSL + Win11 (miniQMT):
    WSL runs our code (our stock data is local too), updates the local database (I currently use my JoinQuant account to update it) and searches for promising stocks.
    If miniQMT is no longer offered and only full QMT is, we have to use the broker's software (running on Win11) and set up a local API server to access the local program.

2 Our trading system could use machine learning and an AI agent (hermes) for data analysis, financial-report analysis and a data feedback loop, but I do not yet know how to introduce this part.

3 A more complex strategy is not a better strategy, and historical data must not be over-relied on (otherwise the model easily overfits). The stock market is a zero-sum game: when someone makes money someone else loses it, and a strategy
    that makes money now will not make money forever; once its time-sensitivity is gone it stops earning. How do we keep our strategies from becoming over-complex while letting them evolve automatically with the market?
4 We currently trade stocks; in the future there may be funds and bonds. What belongs in the quant software and what belongs in the software architecture? You can also refer to open-source
  quant architectures, but they must meet our requirements as far as possible.
5 Once you have a solution, organize the current architecture; I need to sync changes across different computers via GitHub.

What I summarized may contain contradictions; please evaluate a feasible plan on the basis of a sound quant architecture. Write an evolution document and we will execute it step by step.

Our GitHub remote address:  git@github.com:com0do/quant.git
